# /etc/cron.d/watchfor-agent — the one-shot variant for hosts without a
# long-running service (or where a daemon is not wanted). `once` collects two
# samples a second apart (rates need both), pushes one batch and exits; the
# spool catches up if the server was unreachable. Cron cannot go below a
# minute; the plan minimum applies on top of that, so every minute is fine.
* * * * * watchfor-agent /usr/local/bin/watchfor-agent once -config /etc/watchfor-agent/agent.yml
